from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib
root=Path('prototypes/low-profile-b');data=json.loads((root/'colour-samples.json').read_text());data['reference_sha256']=hashlib.sha256((root/'reference.jpg').read_bytes()).hexdigest();(root/'colour-samples.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{html.escape(k.replace("_"," "))}</td><td><span class="swatch" style="background:{v["hex"]}"></span><code>{v["hex"]}</code></td><td>{v["box"]}</td></tr>' for k,v in data['regions'].items())
pairs=''.join(f'<section><h2>{title}</h2><a href="compare-{name}.png"><img class="pair" src="compare-{name}.png" alt="Original mockup and actual Prototype B {name} at equal scale"></a></section>' for name,title in [('knobs','Knob proportions, pointers and actual value arcs'),('mixer','Mixer slots and compact dark caps'),('buttons','Dark rectangular switches and selected LED'),('screen','Recessed glass and live-display styling'),('cheek','Flat side housing and material contrast')])
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>GRIMISS Prototype B — reference comparison and approval</title><style>body{background:#0b0e0c;color:#cbd8d0;font:15px system-ui;margin:0}main{max-width:1320px;margin:auto;padding:28px 20px}h1{font-size:25px;color:#50efd5}h2{font-size:19px;margin-top:32px}p{max-width:1050px;line-height:1.65}a{color:#50efd5}img{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto}.hero{width:1280px}.pair{width:auto}section{padding:8px 0 20px;border-bottom:1px solid #293a31}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}th,td{padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #34463b;text-align:left}.swatch{display:inline-block;width:35px;height:18px;border:1px solid #607568;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:12px}.notice{border-left:3px solid #50efd5;background:#111814;padding:14px 18px}.links{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:20px 0}code{font-size:12px}</style><main><h1>Hardware Section Prototype B — approved refinements</h1><p class="notice">Prototype A was rejected. This is an isolated replacement study, not a rollout to the synthesizer. The existing synth, audio engine, MIDI and parameter bindings remain unchanged. Prototype B was approved with brighter screens, visible bezels and heavier screen-printed lettering throughout. Those refinements are shown here; the component design is now used in the full instrument.</p><nav class="links"><a href="board.html">Open interactive Prototype B</a><a href="browser-full.png">Full-resolution browser screenshot · 1600×900</a><a href="browser-section.png">Browser section screenshot</a><a href="reference.jpg">Original supplied mockup</a></nav><section><h2>Actual browser capture</h2><a href="browser-section.png"><img class="hero" src="browser-section.png" alt="Prototype B browser screenshot with near-black surfaces, flat graphite housings and bright value arcs"></a><p>Compact, relatively flat black knob tops and shallow sidewalls replace the smooth domed/disc treatment. A dark inactive arc and a bright value-driven active arc are separate elements. Teal, magenta and amber remain distinct. Flat graphite end housings replace tubular rails; green is limited to dark display glass, subtle panel undertones and controlled edge lighting.</p></section><section><h2>Direct reference sampling</h2><p>These are per-channel medians of rectangles from the supplied1280×640JPEG, with coordinates retained for audit. Surfaces and illuminated areas were sampled separately. The face sample is near black with a slight green undertone; the cheek face is neutral graphite. Cabinet paint is a restrained near-neutral charcoal, with no broad green gradient. JPEG lighting is not treated as a uniform material colour. The original mAMB accent colours are retained for live value indicators.</p><table><tr><th>Reference region</th><th>Sample median</th><th>Source rectangle [left, top, right, bottom]</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table><p><a href="colour-samples.json">Sampling data and original-image SHA256</a> · <a href="verification.json">Browser verification</a></p></section><section><h2>Matched-scale reference comparison</h2><p>Left: unchanged crops from the original supplied mockup. Right: crops from the actual browser screenshot. Both sides use the same2×pixel enlargement, with no independent fitting, stretching, colour adjustment or retouching. Open a comparison PNG for its full pixel dimensions. On a narrow screen the complete pair scales together.</p></section>'''+pairs+'''<section><h2>Original reference — complete image</h2><a href="reference.jpg"><img src="reference.jpg" width="1280" height="640" alt="Original approved GRIMISS hardware mockup supplied by the user"></a></section><p>Chromium checks passed for arc positions at0/25/50/100%, mouse dragging and display response, compact cap movement, switch LED selection, preserved accent colours and in-panel controls. This visual prototype contains no audio engine. The prototype remains isolated from audio/MIDI; the approved component design is now used in the full interface. Approved component direction, updated with the requested screen glow, bezels and heavier screen-printed lettering throughout.</p></main></html>'''
(root/'index.html').write_text(page)
